{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:93461",
  "title": "Important: util-linux security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-03 12:10:03"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-07 00:12:48"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The util-linux packages contain a large variety of low-level system utilities that are necessary for a Linux system to function. Among others, these include the fdisk configuration tool and the login program.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program when setting up loop devices (CVE-2026-27456)\n\n* util-linux: util-linux: heap use-after-free in libblkid nested partition probing (CVE-2026-13595)\n\n* util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program via ancestor directory swap on target path (CVE-2026-53613)\n\n* util-linux: util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program when applying post-mount ownership/mode changes (CVE-2026-53612)\n\n* util-linux: util-linux: SUID mount(8) allows nosuid/noexec bypass via LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2 (CVE-2026-53614)\n\n* util-linux: util-linux: failed external mount helper still runs privileged X-mount post-hooks (CVE-2026-76642)\n\n* util-linux: util-linux: nsenter --join-cgroup leaks root cgroup migration authority (CVE-2026-78408)\n\n* util-linux: util-linux: restricted bind mounts do not pin the source, allowing X-mount.owner/group/mode redirection (CVE-2026-78410)\n\n* util-linux: util-linux: Partition metadata compromise via integer overflow in DOS partition parser (CVE-2026-53615)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
